  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* Text that shipped as template literals (BACKLOG-0001106).        */
  /*                                                                  */
  /* The build check matched only single-quoted literals at a sink,   */
  /* so a `${name} not in view` or a `const` holding the text was     */
  /* never seen, and each of these reached every locale in English.   */
  /* The presence refusal is the one that matters most: it is a live  */
  /* region, so a screen-reader user in any other language heard a    */
  /* refused edit announced in English. English seeded; awaiting      */
  /* human translation in the other catalogues (see i18n.test.js).    */
  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------- */

  // Presence: the roster's note for peers whose rows this view is not
  // showing, and the refusal announcement with its stand-in for an unnamed
  // peer. A plural object even though the English does not inflect, because
  // the languages that do must be able to.
