    // grid — which is what the first version did, and it did not work. A
    // tooltip raised by hovering leaves focus wherever it was, usually on
    // `<body>`, so a key press never reaches a listener inside the grid at all.
    // WCAG 1.4.13 requires the content to be dismissible *without moving the
    // pointer*, so the listener has to be somewhere the key will actually
    // arrive. Capture, so this transient bubble gets first refusal ahead of the
    // editor, the menu and the maximised view — each of which checks
    // `defaultPrevented` — and it consumes the key only while a tooltip is
    // actually open, so Escape behaves exactly as before the rest of the time.
